      "body": "## What\nIn the Metal kernels README, three link labels named `sgl-kernel/setup_metal.py` and `sgl-kernel/tests/`, but the top-level `sgl-kernel/` directory no longer exists. I changed the labels to `python/sglang/kernels/aot/setup_metal.py` and `python/sglang/kernels/aot/tests/`. The link targets were already correct.\n\n## Why\nA small, objectively-verifiable improvement (docs) found during a\ndaily open-source maintenance pass (2026-10-17).\n\n## How verified\n`ls sgl-kernel/setup_metal.py` fails, so the old directory is gone. The link targets `../../setup_metal.py` and `../../tests` resolve to `python/sglang/kernels/aot/`, where `setup_metal.py` exists. `git ls-files tests` shows tracked files under `tests/`. `git diff --stat` shows 3 insertions and 3 deletions in 1 file. I did not run a link checker or a docs build.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39023981983](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39023981983)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39023981976](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39023981976)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39023981987](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39023981987)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
